# The texas-exam-prep/ directory is a SEPARATE Next.js application with its own
# package.json, its own dependencies and its own CI workflow. It is not part of
# this app and must not be uploaded to or built by this project's deployment.
#
# Without this, Vercel's build type-checks the whole repository against THIS
# app's tsconfig, where the `@/*` path alias points at the repository root.
# Every `@/components/...` import inside texas-exam-prep then resolves to a
# path that does not exist here, and the build fails with a few hundred
# "cannot find module" errors that have nothing to do with this application.
#
# tsconfig.json excludes the directory as well. Both are needed: the tsconfig
# exclude is what fixes the type check, and this file stops the source being
# uploaded at all.
texas-exam-prep
